      "writtenOn": "2021-03-16T13:18:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAICT this method uses in-band signaling to tell whether a path is:\n\n- A Soong output path (if it starts with out/soong)\n- An output path (if it starts with out/)\n- A source path (anything else)\n\nAn alternative would be to use out-of-band signaling and have assertion methods like\n\nAssertSourcePath(...)\nAssertOutPath(...)\nAssertSoongOutPath(...)\n\nIt would look a bit nicer (in-band signaling is icky because what if e.g. you have out/Android.bp), but:\n\n- You\u0027d need a 3x more assertion methods\n- The cases where you currently pass a []string as a set of expected paths would become complicated if you want to pass in a mixture of source and output paths.\n\nIs this similar to your reasons for choosing in-band signaling here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 896,
        "startChar": 5,
